TWICE CAUGHT BY THE SAME TRAP
  Both attempts to do this inline through pwsh -Command failed to parse: the Chinese full-width quotes
  inside a double-quoted string were treated as string delimiters. The fix was to write the whole thing
  as a .ps1 file (UTF-8 with BOM) with every Chinese literal in a single-quoted string, then run the file.
  This is the third time in this conversation that non-ASCII literals have broken an inline command; the
  durable lesson is that any script containing Chinese quotes or full-width punctuation should go to a
  file, not into -Command.
